{"seconds": 3.161221583141014, "submission_file": "experiments/generation-repairs-v1/submissions/K04/gpt-5-2025-08-07/r2.json", "submission_sha256": "e36c4bf4ddd99f2722b672dd0ad9b49987bd1936559a92c627610b98f9fc3314", "code_sha256": "f07cfddaf750a51775c1b4985eb2530cdc1956329ee22f346265f478c4905aff", "description": "Supervised donor-held-out transfer from expression to cortical layers. Genes are already the 500 outer-training variance-selected non-mitochondrial features and have identical order in train/test. Pipeline:\n- Per-gene z-score using only training data (mean/std). No test-fit or any neighbor/batch adaptation; fixed per-row computation only arises from this linear transform.\n- Multinomial Logistic Regression (solver=saga, L2) with deterministic seed. Sample weights balance both class imbalance and donor imbalance: weight = class_weight(y) * group_weight(donor), where each donor contributes equally and classes are inversely proportional to their training frequency. This also makes the CV robust to folds missing some classes.\n- Hyperparameter C is chosen by GroupKFold over donors (2 folds). For each fold, the scaler is refit on the fold\u2019s training split only; macro-F1 across all seven labels [0..6] with zero_division=0 is averaged across folds. Missing classes in a fold are handled naturally (no training samples \u2192 no weights for that class; evaluation still includes all 7 labels).\n- Final model is retrained on all training donors with the chosen C and the training-only scaler, then predicts argmax labels for the test spots.\nThe method uses only expression, respects grouped validation by donor, avoids any test-driven selection/normalization, and outputs one integer label 0..6 per test row.", "code_lines": 99, "line_limit_compliant": true, "line_limit_exclusive": 240}

